# Everything in log/ stays private EXCEPT log/learnings/ -- that one's a real
# submission deliverable (assignment 2, section 2.2's confident-wrong-path docs)
# and needs to be visible on GitHub. `log/*` + a negation, not just `!log/learnings/`
# on its own -- git won't look inside a fully-excluded parent directory to find
# negation matches, so the parent has to be excluded one level shallow instead.
log/*
!log/learnings/

